            <ArticleTitle>Chest pain caused by tracheostomy tube malposition: the importance of choosing the right tube.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>231-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of chest pain caused by tracheostomy tube malposition in a 65-year old woman with chronic respiratory failure due to chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. This report highlights the importance of the correct choice of tracheostomy tube devices for mechanically ventilated and/or spontaneously breathing patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
